Description:
IS/M, Inc.- Industrial Sales / Marketing, is an experienced SPECIFICATION driven, Manufacturers Representative, covering the Southeast, with offices located in;

Richmond,VA. , Raleigh, NC., Greenville, SC. ,  Montgomery, AL. , and Melbourne, FL.

Our Field Service & Sales personnel have both practical and hands on application experience with a variety of products including;  Motor / Generator Brushes, Spring Clips, Brush Holders, Commutator Tools / Supplies, Shaft Grounding Devices.  Wireless Plant Monitoring / Preventive Maintenance Components / Systems, Hot Spot Monitoring, Motor Bearing Temperature and Vibration Sensing.  Explosion Proof Devices.  Machine Guarding Devices, Interlocks, RFID Interlocks, Cable Switches, Light Curtains.  AC / DC Drives, Shaft Speed Monitoring, Photo Electric / Proximity Sensors, Palm Buttons, Thru-Door Programming Ports, 600 / 4160 Voltage Indicators, Lock Out Tag Out, PESD’s (Permanent Electrical Safety Devices), Enclosures / Cabinets, Stainless Cable Entry glands, Cord Grips and Multi-conductor Cord Sets.  Rectangular / Round connectors, Fiber Optic, Ethernet IP and Ethernet Switches, Custom Cable Assemblies.

Viewtech is an Italian manufacturer of vision inspection systems for the quality control of food packaging.

Viewtech solutions verify and certify the quality of many industrial products such as:
 - food packages: sliced products trays, steak trays, flat pouches or cans;
 - seals, gaskets, technical pieces;
 - pharma packages;

Performed controls by Viewtech equipment include:
 - seal integrity;
 - printed data position and correctness: expiry date, batch code, product number;
 - barcode position and correctness;
 - label position and conformity;
 - label integrity;
 - top film and labe(s) congruity
 - product quality;

Despite being a relatively young business, Viewtech already reached a groundbreaking position in the development and application of this technology and is now relating with companies on an international level, within a highly globalised market, where the quality of products and services is now above and beyond the standards.

Tool and Die Company established in 1970.  Specializing in the following types of metal stamping dies;
hand fed, progressive, deep draw, high finish, compound, transfer and computerized.
We also make special machines including computer controlled devices.

Our Design team  provides a complete integrated design of process, mechanical, electrical and instrumentation systems required to implement the process strategy.  We can provide you with planning and design to help you on capital projects both new and revamp to assure the purchasing of equipment and installation processes stay on schedule.   We also provide complete Control System design and integration to make your process run efficiently and reduce possibility of operator error.  Automatic recording of process data will help you keep your process running its best.

Our staff has worked on hundreds of projects in the following industries;

Specialitly Chemicals • Foods • Polymerization • Textile • Brewing • Dyestuffs • Power • Plastics • Pharmaceuticals • Pulp & Paper • Waste Treatment • Petrochemical • Material Handling • Minerals • Extrusion & drying

EAE Tech specializes in providing electrical power distribution systems, automation and process control systems, quality engineered products, electrical and controls engineering services, and installation solutions that provide our customers with operational upgrades and/or improvements based on their project needs.

EAE Tech’s technical strengths go well beyond the traditional PLC/SCADA controls of other system integrators.

We are a full‐service electrical design group and will work with your team to develop your scope, schedule and budget during the preliminary engineering project Phase (PEP), provide consulting engineering services, or design and provide comprehensive industrial electrical systems ranging from outdoor substations to Level 1 PLC/HMI control systems. Additionally, our highly skilled and experienced personnel are very comfortable coordinating from the field to the control room. We can develop the detailed electrical installation package, supervise and/or hire the electrical contractor for the installation phase.

Owner’s benefit from having one company that provides value engineering with tightly integrated power distribution and automation systems. This synergy reduces the design/delivery cycle, reduces electrical installation costs, and provides seamless project execution which mitigates coordination issues and risk.

Our competent staff can provide project, supplemental or turn‐key solutions depending on your specific project needs. Below is a more detailed explanation of EAE Tech’s capabilities.

Engineering Services Include

- Project development and management including estimation, scope writing and scheduling;
- Controls/automation hardware design, fabrication and witness testing (customers encouraged to attend);
- PLC, SCADA and database software design & programming (familiar with most PLC/SCADA manufacturers);
- Complete power distribution system coordination & design from 138kV and below (with integrated controls);
